	in API PATCH /pets/{petId}
		the request required property `allOf[subschema #3]/릇䍱琨압蝪颯` became read-only
		This is a warning because a read-only property should not be sent in a request, and the specification leaves it to the server whether to ignore it or reject the request. Clients that send it may be rejected, or find the value they send is no longer used. This compared the `allOf` branches one at a time, so another branch may still guarantee what this one dropped. Run with --flatten-allof to merge the branches and compare what they describe together.


